{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1481677-aberrant-\u201ccore\u201d-campaign-arc","id":1481677,"title":"Aberrant - \u201cCore\u201d Campaign Arc","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-22T11:20:25-07:00","id":1481677,"title":"Aberrant - \u201cCore\u201d Campaign Arc","content":"So I am thinking about how to structure an Aberrant campaign in the new edition. One thing the old edition had was a very clear structure for a campaign arc to build around - solving Slider\u2019s murder, uncovering and defeating the conspiracy. You can debate how effectively the old campaign books pulled this off, but there was a core storyline built into Aberrant, with a hypothetical climax and resolution you could reach in the campaign. <br /> <br /> Now, don\u2019t get me wrong, I understand why the new edition removed that element, and I don\u2019t necessarily disagree with the decision. It\u2019s a very 90s concept, and there are plausibility issues that have been picked over for decades at this point. <br /> <br /> So I get why that element was removed. But it doesn\u2019t seem to have been replaced with anything in particular in the new edition.<br /> <br /> I am curious if anyone sees an equivalent \u201cbuilt in\u201d story structure to build a campaign around in the new edition - or if you have created your own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T18:39:06-07:00","id":1481707,"title":"","content":"There is no equivalent built in story structure to follow. It is more like a sand box with many different hooks to place your campaign.<br /> <br /> There are more than a few options reading through the first few chapters of the book, from local crime fighting, to combating prejudice of many kinds, to fight someone else wars to profit on it, to the big fight Utopia x Teragen (yet more philosophical, but warming up in the next decade or so).<br /> <br /> I personally like the idea of S\u00e3o Paulo blast investigation, but it has no direction to start if you go that way, instead it has many hooks to cling too\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T01:36:22-07:00","id":1481833,"title":"","content":"I always figured with Aberrant players would direct the story. You have so much power. Play a group of Nova's in Hollywood trying to revitalize the Hollywood movie industry. Try to make your hometown an industrial and technological powerhouse. Explore space. Create a philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T13:19:54-07:00","id":1482647,"title":"","content":"The first edition of Aberrant was (for better or worse) a product of its time both in substance--standing as a cynical GenX critique of 90's celebrity culture and globalization--and in context--the revolution of &quot;games as art&quot; and when Metaplots Roamed the Earth.<br /> <br /> This edition, almost by necessity, had to break from the old as its themes and design hadn't kept up with the times. So, if there can be said to be a &quot;core&quot; plot, it would most likely have to be in the context of the emergence of Quantum Flux and its evolution (degredation?) into Quantum Corruption, and the ultimate failure of Michael Donigal's dream.<br /> <br /> But this edition also stands apart by explicitly laying out that there is no &quot;one path&quot;, no fixed fate. Slider isn't some girl in a refrigerator for the PCs to avenge. Ceastus Pax is a completely different character. Corbin is... okay, he's still the same. But they're all off doing their own thing, and as novas, people of consequence wether they like it or not, the PCs should take the lead, too.<br /> <br /> So, to answer the question, No. There isn't, and there doesn't need to be. You have power; it's not &quot;bad wrong fun&quot; to use it, you just have to be willing to pay the price. I haven't come up with my own, yet, as I'm still running my group through an Aeon campaign. And the idea of what they would do with Aberrant's level of power frankly terrifies me. I'll probably run something safer for my sanity next time, like W:tA.<br /> <br /> I've also been reading through Claremont's X-Men run lately, and the idea of an anti-terrorist nova team launching surgical strikes from an abandoned ghost town in the Australian Outback tickles me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25998-loneshark","name":"Loneshark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T16:49:31-07:00","id":1482856,"title":"","content":"I like Aberrant 2e better than Aberrant 1e precisely because it\u2019s so open ended, but that\u2019s just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T07:28:05-07:00","id":1483373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loneshark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1481677-aberrant-\u201ccore\u201d-campaign-arc?p=1482647#post1482647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first edition of Aberrant was (for better or worse) a product of its time both in substance--standing as a cynical GenX critique of 90's celebrity culture and globalization--and in context--the revolution of &quot;games as art&quot; and when Metaplots Roamed the Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't particularly disagree with this as a critique of the 1st edition metaplot/campaign arc. I don't really think the original game's 'core' plot would work today. <br /> <br /> At the same time, I will fully admit that right now the main thing stopping me running the game is that I haven't been able to come up with a great concept for what I'll do with it instead. Aberrant is trickier than almost any other superhero game, precisely because a lot of the traditional superhero tropes don't really exist in the setting either. In a traditional superhero game, the game structure is ultimately built on 'A Supervillain is Doing Something, Go Beat Them Up.' <br /> <br /> In Aberrant - at least in the default setting, assuming you don't crank up the 4-Color Genre dial - the Teragen aren't launching a hypno-ray to hold the Earth hostage. Novas don't rob banks, because they can make far more money through legit means. It's a superhero game with (mostly) no supervillains. <br /> <br /> Which is cool! It's what I like about Aberrant!<br /> <br /> But it means you need to replace &quot;Let's go raid the island of Dr. Destroyer&quot; with something else for the players to actually deal with. In the first edition, the game provided an answer to that question - in the default game mode, you're part of a nova resistance trying to expose an anti-nova conspiracy. I'm struggling a bit with what to replace that with now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T08:17:17-07:00","id":1483378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1481677-aberrant-\u201ccore\u201d-campaign-arc?p=1483373#post1483373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it means you need to replace &quot;Let's go raid the island of Dr. Destroyer&quot; with something else for the players to actually deal with. In the first edition, the game provided an answer to that question - in the default game mode, you're part of a nova resistance trying to expose an anti-nova conspiracy. I'm struggling a bit with what to replace that with now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some other elements you could play with that (I'm pretty sure) still linger;<br /> -Bigots from the Church of Michael Archangel still roam the earth making the lives of novas miserable with their incessant faith-based hatred, and they will infiltrate every level of government to try to remove the &quot;nova threat&quot;.<br /> -Elite warfare is still a thing, and there's little stopping a nova from carving their own nation from some 3rd world country as a dictator.<br /> -The methodology of the Aberrant faction of terats (previously Nova Vigilance + Harvesters) has not changed, and they will use disproportionate force to avenge any crime against novakind<br /> -Whether it wants to admit this or not, the USA still wants a nationalist nova force to compete with the others (who most assuredly exist within rival nations), even if they can't justify the budgeting that would require.<br /> <br /> Also a note about the new setting, nova population is like 1/10th what it was in the first edition, so now ANY nova is more valuable as a commodity. And all extant power players in the world will be scrambling to find a way to acquire as many as possible just to have them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T09:14:30-07:00","id":1483380,"title":"","content":"And there's nothing saying that you can't bring back a form of the 1e metaplot; just present it as a rogue faction within Proteus instead of being approved by Proteus leadership; and present it as something that started out as a response to the Terat that got out of hand, rather than as something that was always intended to be targeted at Novas in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}